From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 11:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r25-1-0079: add unified RenderProgram backend interface

Start unified-backend generation 1 from the r25 + 0051 + 0075-0076
ownership and parser-order baseline. Deliberately do not apply or call the
0077/0078 legacy path-display-list consumers.

Add one internal holder-level execution contract for normal, mixed-content,
and path-heavy rendering. The contract defines complete-result semantics and
a value-only metrics schema for program/index construction, candidate query,
compile, replay, raster, blend, dispatch, and bounded memory accounting.

This revision is behavior-neutral. The implementation always returns
kDisabled, has no render-path call site, allocates no storage, takes no lock,
emits no log, and changes no pixel. It reports only already-owned RenderProgram
command/byte metadata when an explicit future benchmark calls it. Canonical
PDFium and the existing r25 renderer remain authoritative.

Later r25-1 patches must extend this single contract rather than adding another
display list, scheduler, spatial index, cache owner, or destination bitmap.
